.TH LSEEK 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
lseek \- change the file offset of a descriptor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.PP
.BI "off_t lseek(int " descriptor ", off_t " offset ", int " whence ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR lseek ()
changes the open file's offset by a signed byte
.I offset
relative to the position selected by
.IR whence .
.B SEEK_SET
selects the beginning,
.B SEEK_CUR
the current offset, and
.B SEEK_END
the end of the file.
These constants are declared in
.BR <unistd.h> .
Seeking beyond the end does not itself extend the file.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The resulting byte offset is returned on success.
On failure, \-1 is returned and
.B errno
is set to the positive Linux error number.
Successful calls leave
.B errno
unchanged.
.SH ERRORS
Include
.B <errno.h>
to inspect
.BR errno .
Possible errors include
.B EBADF
for an invalid descriptor,
.B EINVAL
for an invalid origin or resulting offset, and
.B ESPIPE
for a pipe or another nonseekable descriptor.
Other Linux
.BR lseek (2)
errors are possible.
.SH NOTES
The offset and result use Crunch's signed 64\-bit
.BR long .
This Crunch library function is linked from
.BR libcrunch.a ;
its
.B errno
is process\-wide, not thread\-local.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR open (3crunch),
.BR read (3crunch),
.BR write (3crunch),
.BR lseek (2)
